<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><description>Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 15:36:54 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category></category><title>US woman who survived botched execution is conscious, speaking</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261007-us-woman-who-survived-botched-execution-is-conscious-speaking</link><description>
The woman who survived a failed execution in a US prison last week is now conscious and speaking, but her prognosis remains unclear, her lawyers said on Tuesday. Christa Pike, 50, who was sentenced to death for a murder she committed when she was a teenager, received two supposedly lethal doses of the drug pentobarbital at a Tennessee prison a week ago.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/48bfc93a-c23e-11f1-94b7-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261007-121149-121309-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/48bfc93a-c23e-11f1-94b7-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261007-121149-121309-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4da46dca-c23e-11f1-8a36-c1cc290b9724</guid><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 14:28:58 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Scars from Oct. 7 fuel deep divisions over Netanyahu ahead of Israeli election</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261007-scars-from-oct-7-fuel-deep-divisions-over-netanyahu-ahead-of-israeli-election</link><description>
As Israel gears up for its first elections since Hamas' Oct. 7, 2023, attack, Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and his opponents are putting it at the heart of their campaigns. Three years on, the worst security failure in Israel’s history now threatens to end the career of its longest-serving prime minister. FRANCE 24's Noga Tarnopolsky reports from Jerusalem.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/02825e94-c25a-11f1-bf55-b942c38e4bd7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261007-160619-160824-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/02825e94-c25a-11f1-bf55-b942c38e4bd7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261007-160619-160824-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">08099a76-c25a-11f1-b5e4-39de3d8610d4</guid><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 14:23:22 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>African tourists cancelling trip as xenophobia shadows South Africa's appeal</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261007-african-tourists-cancelling-trip-as-xenophobia-shadows-south-africa-s-appeal</link><description>
South Africa has recorded record tourist arrivals over the past two months, with more than one million visitors arriving by air each month. But behind these encouraging figures, a concern is emerging: African tourists may gradually turn away from South Africa, even as tourism accounts for more than 8% of the country’s GDP. The country’s xenophobic image has left its mark, as FRANCE 24’s team on the ground reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d392bdfe-c259-11f1-8a14-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261006-215333-215539-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d392bdfe-c259-11f1-8a14-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261006-215333-215539-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d8777c88-c259-11f1-b839-a1966c2a7f9c</guid><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 14:22:11 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Brit adventurer back on UK soil after 28-year round-the-world walk</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261007-brit-adventurer-back-on-uk-soil-after-28-year-round-the-world-walk</link><description>
British adventurer on a 50,000-kilometre, 28-year trek home from South America without using any transport has set foot on UK soil after swimming the Channel, his publicists said Tuesday. Karl Bushby, a 57-year-old former paratrooper, set off from Punta Arenas, Chile, in November 1998, vowing to reach his mother's home near Hull in northern England without travelling on planes, trains, boats, vehicles or other transport modes.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2015408c-c257-11f1-b067-b942c38e4bd7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261007-154104-154227-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2015408c-c257-11f1-b067-b942c38e4bd7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261007-154104-154227-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">24c7d644-c257-11f1-85a8-c5214af9e234</guid><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 14:19:06 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>New Comoros law bans foreign nationals from certain jobs</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261007-new-comoros-law-bans-foreign-nationals-from-certain-jobs</link><description>
A new law in the Comoros bans foreign nationals from running certain small-scale businesses, threatening the livelihoods of thousands of people, most of them Malagasy. A measure that mirrors a growing wave of economic protectionism targeting migrant workers across the continent.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1c029bfa-c259-11f1-a6e3-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261006-214820-215032-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1c029bfa-c259-11f1-a6e3-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261006-214820-215032-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">22058ec2-c259-11f1-bfc1-39de3d8610d4</guid><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 14:17:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>arts24</category><title>A new 'Les Mis': This week in French film</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261007-a-new-les-mis-this-week-in-french-film</link><description>
This week on arts24, film critic Manon Kerjean takes us through some of the latest French cinema releases, starting with a new adaptation of Victor Hugo's "Les Misérables". Vincent Lindon plays Jean Valjean, opposite Tahar Rahim as Inspector Javert in a three-hour epic that brings a thriller-like tension to the classic story. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/96e209d0-c23d-11f1-8540-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/DLS-AFF-FOND-CINEMA-LES-MISERABLES-frame-708.jpeg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/96e209d0-c23d-11f1-8540-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/DLS-AFF-FOND-CINEMA-LES-MISERABLES-frame-708.jpeg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a5b24eac-c23d-11f1-a565-89f8849797b8</guid><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 14:12:35 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Eve JACKSON</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>What we know about espionage, treason allegations against Germany's ex-spy chief</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261007-what-we-know-about-espionage-treason-allegations-against-germany-s-ex-spy-chief</link><description>
A court on Wednesday ordered the former head of Germany's foreign intelligence service August Hanning to remain in pretrial detention after his arrest on suspicion of espionage and treason, along with a former deputy who allegedly supplied him with secret files. Here's what we know about one of the biggest security breaches in German history.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/498bd9a8-c257-11f1-bb2c-b942c38e4bd7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25254411016248.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/498bd9a8-c257-11f1-bb2c-b942c38e4bd7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25254411016248.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">60a7173a-c255-11f1-b4b7-ed2219ea2917</guid><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 14:06:59 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/498bd9a8-c257-11f1-bb2c-b942c38e4bd7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25254411016248.jpg">© Liesa Johannssen, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>From Mai 68 to 2026: France’s long student protests tradition</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261007-from-mai-68-to-2026-france-s-long-student-protests-tradition</link><description>
Students, parents and trade unions were demonstrating across France Tuesday, protesting what they say is under-investment in high schools. From Mai 68 to the CPE crisis in 2006, major French student and youth protests have pressured leaders and transformed national politics.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/46d28730-c256-11f1-8b0c-b942c38e4bd7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261007-153338-153555-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/46d28730-c256-11f1-8b0c-b942c38e4bd7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261007-153338-153555-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4fe43eae-c256-11f1-8964-1519407c02f5</guid><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 13:57:04 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>The secrets behind Mali junta’s takeover of Kidal without a fight</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261007-russia-backed-mali-junta-retakes-strategic-town-after-separatists-withdraw</link><description>
The Malian army says it has entered the strategic northern city of Kidal, which was captured around five months ago by Tuareg separatists who announced their withdrawal earlier Tuesday as the military advanced – a symbolic boost to Mali's junta and its Russian backers. In late April, jihadists from Al-Qaeda-linked JNIM and its Tuareg separatist allies kicked off a series of attacks aimed at weakening Mali's junta rulers, including taking control of Kidal and killing the defence minister. FRANCE 24’s Senior journalist Wassim Nasr explains.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c3d814ee-c255-11f1-a7c8-ff8cff4603f0/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261007-152258-152916-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c3d814ee-c255-11f1-a7c8-ff8cff4603f0/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261007-152258-152916-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ca244494-c255-11f1-8063-83cb21b2a8bc</guid><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 13:55:40 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Entre Nous</category><title>Why American artist Mary Cassatt's legacy still resonates in France today</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261007-why-american-artist-mary-cassatt-s-legacy-still-resonates-in-france-today</link><description>
In this edition we're pleased to welcome back Lauren Jimerson to discuss the Mary Cassatt exhibit entitled "The Choice of Independence" that's currently showing at the Musee d'Orsay in Paris. Lauren is an art historian and author, specialising in modern art and women artists. She tells us why Cassatt was a key figure in the Impressionist movement and why this exhibition is so important. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/048fe212-c249-11f1-9d52-ff8cff4603f0/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-15590507656ac63844a15e43-96531023.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/048fe212-c249-11f1-9d52-ff8cff4603f0/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-15590507656ac63844a15e43-96531023.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7080820c-c248-11f1-9b6a-db2563bdf2ff</guid><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 13:52:42 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Delano D’SOUZA</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Russia warns against spreading 'false information' as reports emerge of second plague case</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261007-russia-warns-against-spreading-false-information-reports-emerge-second-plague-case</link><description>
The World Health Organization joined Western leaders on Wednesday in urging Russia to share more information about what killed a plague institute worker in Siberia as reports emerged of a second suspected case. The Kremlin said Moscow had shared what it knew and accused the media ​of spreading "false information".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/59435228-c24c-11f1-ac27-ff8cff4603f0/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26278372667862.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/59435228-c24c-11f1-ac27-ff8cff4603f0/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26278372667862.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a82b71d0-c24d-11f1-b60f-fd2056609791</guid><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 13:43:19 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/59435228-c24c-11f1-ac27-ff8cff4603f0/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26278372667862.jpg">© AP, Handout Irkutsk Anti-Plague Research Institute of Siberia and Far East</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>China's evolving funeral practices: From traditional burials to cremation</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261007-china-s-evolving-funeral-practices-from-traditional-burials-to-cremation</link><description>
This year, China released new rules for funeral practices. The government is putting an emphasis on affordable and environmentally friendly funeral services. It's part of a decades-long reform to promote cremation. But in a country where burials are deeply rooted in local traditions, how are these attempts to modernise funerals being perceived? FRANCE 24's Yena Lee reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3ab7a90a-c254-11f1-a547-0f96b136895a/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-16941364316ac64b13f2aa21-12033295.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3ab7a90a-c254-11f1-a547-0f96b136895a/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-16941364316ac64b13f2aa21-12033295.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c5895e6e-c1a2-11f1-8ae1-e1c42347efde</guid><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 13:39:24 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Yena LEE</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>'Great moral courage: The French thought they knew de Gaulle and suddenly realized they didn't'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261007-great-moral-courage-the-french-thought-they-knew-de-gaulle-and-suddenly-realized-they-didn-t</link><description>
François Picard is pleased to welcome Julian Jackson, the British historian, author and Emeritus Professor of Modern French History at Queen Mary University of London. His biography of General de Gaulle laid the foundation for France’s two-part biopic, "De Gaulle: Résistance". And on the heels of this surprise box-office hit, Jackson’s book is now available in French: La Chute : France 1940. He takes us back to the occupation of Paris and the extraordinary collapse of France in the summer of 1940.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d6575e74-c23f-11f1-9aa6-ff8cff4603f0/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261006-182018-183102-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d6575e74-c23f-11f1-9aa6-ff8cff4603f0/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261006-182018-183102-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0bfbfbb6-c254-11f1-80be-f17cb4323ef1</guid><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 13:36:04 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>October 7: Former Israeli hostage speaks to France 24</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261007-october-7-former-israeli-hostage-speaks-to-france-24</link><description>
“The terrorists pulled us out through the window. They handcuffed me and pushed us into a car that they had brought from Gaza.”
 
Former Israeli hostage Shoshan Haran speaks to France 24.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/158ad354-c255-11f1-9037-0f96b136895a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-ISRAELI-HOSTAGE-tiktok-00-00-12-07-Still004.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/158ad354-c255-11f1-9037-0f96b136895a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-ISRAELI-HOSTAGE-tiktok-00-00-12-07-Still004.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3ea01bca-c253-11f1-9c88-e5b444f805de</guid><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 13:30:20 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>French parents join school protests to support and protect their children</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261007-french-parents-join-school-protests-to-support-and-protect-their-children</link><description>
Widespread protests swept across France on Tuesday over anger at the state of the country's school system. The police responded with tear gas and water canons when some on the fringes of the marches turned violent. Among the demonstrators were parents who came to march alongside their children to support their cause – and, for some, to ensure their children could protest safely. After several teenagers were injured, they feared further clashes.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0169f142-c251-11f1-a899-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261007-144100-144302-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0169f142-c251-11f1-a899-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261007-144100-144302-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">065ac0e6-c251-11f1-8c4d-4312b34599ce</guid><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 13:22:40 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Three years on, October 7 massacre sites in Israel draw visitors seeking to remember</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261007-three-years-on-october-7-massacre-sites-in-israel-draw-visitors-seeking-to-remember</link><description>
Three years after the October 7 attack, when Hamas militants killed at least 1,195 people in Israel – mostly civilians – the sites of the massacre near the Gaza border have become heavily visited memorials. They offer Israelis and Jews in the diaspora a place to honour those who were killed, as FRANCE 24’s Stéphane Amar reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/38fb03d4-c24d-11f1-bbba-0f96b136895a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261007-140154-140340-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/38fb03d4-c24d-11f1-bbba-0f96b136895a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261007-140154-140340-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3dca3344-c24d-11f1-a210-1dbfa900556b</guid><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 13:21:08 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Three years on, questions remain over what Netanyahu knew before October 7</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261007-three-years-on-questions-remain-over-what-netanyahu-knew-before-october-7</link><description>
As Israelis mark the third anniversary of the October 7 Hamas attack, and with elections due later this month, one question keeps resurfacing: What did Benjamin Netanyahu know in the run-up to the attack? The Israeli prime minister has been accused of ignoring repeated warnings – an allegation he denies.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/db8743aa-c24e-11f1-aa94-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261007-140405-140622-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/db8743aa-c24e-11f1-aa94-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261007-140405-140622-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e09e250c-c24e-11f1-b8d8-136affc84249</guid><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 13:18:46 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Devastation in Gaza: Three years of war reshape the enclave beyond recognition</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261007-devastation-in-gaza-three-years-of-war-reshape-the-enclave-beyond-recognition</link><description>
Three years ago, the war between Israel and Hamas began. In Gaza, it has meant three years of bombardment that have dramatically transformed the Palestinian territory. Residents of the enclave try to survive the best they can, caught between hope for a better future and resignation.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2ec24e84-c24f-11f1-98cc-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261007-140653-140851-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2ec24e84-c24f-11f1-98cc-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261007-140653-140851-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">37280596-c24f-11f1-a36f-b3390329c3b1</guid><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 13:17:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>October 7, hour by hour: How the Hamas attack on Israel unfolded</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261007-october-7-hour-by-hour-how-the-hamas-attack-on-israel-unfolded</link><description>
On October 7, 2023, Hamas launched a series of deadly attacks on Israeli towns and military sites near the Gaza border in a massive, coordinated assault. We look back, hour by hour, at how the events unfolded that day and how it has become known as the biggest massacre that the Jewish state has ever seen.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4f380a22-c250-11f1-a4d7-73f176a2394c/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261007-143121-143306-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4f380a22-c250-11f1-a4d7-73f176a2394c/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261007-143121-143306-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">53fc5ee6-c250-11f1-b255-0d0083229740</guid><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 13:15:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French wine output set to hit historic low after record summer heatwaves</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261007-historic-lows-expected-for-french-wine-harvest-after-record-summer-heatwaves</link><description>
The French agriculture ministry on Wednesday forecast a historic low wine output this year after a summer of record high temperatures and a reduction in cultivated areas. The total harvest plunged 14 percent below the 2021–2025 average, with the Champagne region hit hardest due to an early harvest after the heat increased a sugar buildup.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/39a7fc1c-c250-11f1-8d04-73f176a2394c/w:1024/p:16x9/722866d8e235397bf41f0c88ee41b3aac228a160.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/39a7fc1c-c250-11f1-8d04-73f176a2394c/w:1024/p:16x9/722866d8e235397bf41f0c88ee41b3aac228a160.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3a519268-c250-11f1-8c14-4312b34599ce</guid><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 13:08:45 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/39a7fc1c-c250-11f1-8d04-73f176a2394c/w:1024/p:16x9/722866d8e235397bf41f0c88ee41b3aac228a160.jpg">© Gabriel Bouys, AFP (File)</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Perspective</category><title>'Time doesn't heal': Parents of October 7 attacks victim Aner Shapira</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261007-time-doesn-t-heal-parents-of-aner-shapira-killed-on-october-7-2023</link><description>
The parents of a 22-year-old Israeli man who was killed when Hamas attacked the Nova music festival on October 7, 2023 have told FRANCE 24 how they can still feel him surrounding them even though he's no longer here. Shira and Moshe Shapira say that time doesn't heal, but they are learning how to live with their loss. Their son Aner managed to throw seven grenades back towards Hamas fighters, before an eighth exploded in his hands, killing him. They spoke to us in Perspective.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/357ef1f8-c24c-11f1-ac38-0f96b136895a/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-14306598286ac63d9f40c3f4-70504155.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/357ef1f8-c24c-11f1-ac38-0f96b136895a/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-14306598286ac63d9f40c3f4-70504155.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f877ebd4-c23c-11f1-ade5-cdcea157df53</guid><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 12:59:46 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Stuart NORVAL</dc:creator></item><item><category>Business</category><title>Three years after October 7 attacks, Israel's economy shows its strength</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20261007-three-years-after-october-7-attacks-israel-s-economy-shows-its-strength</link><description>
After shrinking briefly in the aftermath of the October 7, 2023 attacks, Israel's GDP is predicted to grow by 4 percent this year. The country's tech sector – specifically its defence startups – has played a big part in this performance but challenges, notably demographic ones, are on the horizon. Meanwhile, the destruction caused by Israel's war in Gaza has reduced GDP per capita in the Palestinian enclave by 83 percent and reconstruction plans there have yet to begin.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d13d4304-c244-11f1-8513-b942c38e4bd7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-7370752796ac631389744e5-02962399.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d13d4304-c244-11f1-8513-b942c38e4bd7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-7370752796ac631389744e5-02962399.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f53c1ac4-c243-11f1-8992-c90f0efd1ca5</guid><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 12:30:26 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Charles PELLEGRIN</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>October 7: Israelis mark three years since Hamas attacks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261007-october-7-israelis-mark-three-years-since-hamas-attacks</link><description>
Israel is marking the third anniversary of the October 7, 2023, Hamas terrorist attack on Wednesday with memorials across the country.
 
At the site of the Nova music festival, where more than 300 people were killed, families gathered at dawn for a moment of silence and paid tribute in front of portraits both of festival-goers and security forces who died on October 7.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bdca8f88-c236-11f1-852d-b942c38e4bd7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26280153593942.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bdca8f88-c236-11f1-852d-b942c38e4bd7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26280153593942.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e43228ae-c23e-11f1-9258-a39aff491d10</guid><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 11:04:39 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France suspends stun grenade use at student protests ahead of PM speech</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261007-france-suspends-stun-grenade-use-at-student-protests-ahead-of-pm-speech</link><description>
France has suspended the use of stun grenades by police at student-led demonstrations, the interior minister said Wednesday, as allegations of police brutality mounted after days of sometimes violent demonstrations across the country. Tens of thousands of people took to the streets across France on Tuesday demanding better conditions in high schools. That same evening, President Emmanuel Macron held an emergency meeting with Prime Minister Sebastien Lecornu and other key ministers to find a way out of the crisis. FRANCE 24's Antonia Kerrigan reports from a high school in Aubervilliers, France.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e592217e-c23c-11f1-956e-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261007-101358-101934-CS-01.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e592217e-c23c-11f1-956e-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261007-101358-101934-CS-01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ea5c7678-c23c-11f1-a645-cdcea157df53</guid><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 10:55:39 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
